{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/52707-raise-dead-questions","id":52707,"title":"Raise Dead Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T13:16:00-08:00","id":52707,"title":"Raise Dead Questions","content":"So, I've got some stuff with Raise Dead that's come up... wondering if I could ask for thoughts or insights!<br /> <br /> Do you think the -1 per day penalty for Raise Dead is implied to come from body decay, or other reasons?<br /> <br /> On that topic, do you imagine that body preservation... either natural (cryogenic) or supernatural (some sorta weird power)... could negate the penalty?<br /> <br /> Could restoring the physical integrity of the body through other means lend 'successes' to such an effort, you think?<br /> <br /> Or alternately, do you imagine the -1 per day is due to some more intangible quality, like 'soul distance'?<br /> <br /> In such a case, could the service of a powerful being who could somehow call such a soul closer mitigate this penalty?<br /> <br /> Does doing the Raise Dead ritual in a bolthole prevent the difficulty from growing by one per day, as it does normally?<br /> <br /> Does storing bodies in a bolthole keep them in 'stasis', not affecting the difficulty?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T16:22:35-08:00","id":52837,"title":"","content":"I think the penalty is mostly because of the decay of the body, with probably a small metaphysical component (the strength of the bond between body and soul).<br /> <br /> Preserving the body could make it easier to resurrect someone, but most preservation methods damage the body, making it even harder to raise the dead.<br /> <br /> As far as I can see Raise Dead is the prime body restoration power, so I wouldn't really allow other powers lending successes (unless you get into the territory of really esoteric powers). Even the Resurrection Numen has the -1 penalty per day, so it seems that equivalent powers also don't help.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, if your players really want to bring Marco Singe back (as you said in your other thread) you could have your players discover a new exploit that enables his ghost to posess a new body completely (living or dead) or that lets him become a Revenant (undead). This way you don't have the problems with the resurrection with a five year old dead body. The only problem is that the players would have to go to the underworld to find his ghost (or if he still lingers, find where he is or if he still lingers), with possible opposition of the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:21:59-08:00","id":52870,"title":"","content":"Since Demon's powers work off of hacking reality. I just assumed that the accumulating -1 was based on the universe's growing acceptance of another corpse. And the difficulty being realigning the person's existence into the whole tapestry as it wore. Of course, it might make for an interesting interlock to make Resurrections easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T22:13:49-08:00","id":55250,"title":"","content":"I generally go with that the -1 is from the cumulative &quot;momentum&quot; the death has in the timeline. If you find a way to step around this (perhaps accessing a splinter in which the person never died, bringing the corpse with you and doing it there, perhaps swapping the alive/dead status between the two copies) then the penalties go out the window, or at least get decreased.<br /> As for ressing someone who has been dead for ages, I'd probably say that's more or less impossible for an angel using anything less than the result of a cipher. (do note though, there are other ways to ress someone than using these things, summoning the ghost from the underworld and shoving them into a living, or dead, human is a good example, and while demons can't do that they could easily enlist others, mages, vampires, werewolves, to do it for them in exchange for secrets or resources)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T01:04:10-08:00","id":55315,"title":"","content":"Our Moros wants to use a Supernal Pact to bring a corpse to its original state, allowing the demon NPC to ressurrect him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T01:09:15-08:00","id":55318,"title":"","content":"Get another demon to use Swift Resolution on the first demon and ignore the penalites!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T01:54:00-08:00","id":55332,"title":"","content":"Well, up to the ST if that would work to remove the penalties. Personally I wouldn't let that work, but the other options are yes and sort of (halved penalties?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:17:03-08:00","id":55338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/52707-raise-dead-questions?p=55332#post55332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, up to the ST if that would work to remove the penalties. Personally I wouldn't let that work, but the other options are yes and sort of (halved penalties?).</div> </div> </div> </div>So how do you interpret the text of Swift Resolution as working?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:27:51-08:00","id":55343,"title":"","content":"I was posting in reply to the Moros trying to make the penalties go away by simply restoring the corpse actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As for Swift Resolution, it doesn't actually negate any penalties, it just makes it so things happen faster (a fair deal actually, extended actions being over in a single roll, fights going automatically to the side with the advantage etc). So, for the, presumably, large penalties involved in ressing someone who has been dead for a considerable amount of time I don't think that one would be of great use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:44:57-08:00","id":55348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/52707-raise-dead-questions?p=55343#post55343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Swift Resolution, it doesn't actually negate any penalties,</div> </div> </div> </div> Raise Dead Doesn't have any penalties to use it, it just requires successes (Sometimes a <u><i><b>lot</b></i></u> of successes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/52707-raise-dead-questions?p=55343#post55343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it just makes it so things happen faster (a fair deal actually, extended actions being over in a single roll, fights going automatically to the side with the advantage etc).</div> </div> </div> </div> If the number of successes required remains the same then Swift Resolution is an exploit to make people fail extended actions; same number of successes, far, far, far fewer dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T03:13:09-08:00","id":55356,"title":"","content":"It sounds like the two of us have been in separate discussions. The penalties in question are the penalties to the Compromise roll, not the mounting successes required.<br /> As for helping with the ressing roll, then yes, that one would, if permitted by GM, be of great use since it would turn it into a &quot;one success required, one roll extended action&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T03:38:48-08:00","id":55362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/52707-raise-dead-questions?p=55356#post55356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like the two of us have been in separate discussions. The penalties in question are the penalties to the Compromise roll, not the mounting successes required.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doh!<br /> <br /> Aren't the penalties modifiers? Modifiers are cumulative, but the total modifier from circumstances should not exceed +/\u20135 dice. Just buy up a high Wits + Manipulation pool (A game about demonic spies that encourages you to be a shrewd, quick-thinking manipulator? Who would have thought it)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T04:06:05-08:00","id":55365,"title":"","content":"Well, personally I wouldn't actually cap that one, for the very reason that if you do something monumental (raise, lets say Hitler... or even someone people have known to bed dead for years) it should be Felt. It might even mean an &quot;automatic&quot; fail on the roll.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting however, I tend to always make sure the effort should be worth it when players do monumental things, so while I might stick the players with a chance roll for ressing that physicist the machine killed last year (if they manage to do so, regardless of method) he'll turn out to be pretty damn useful, and the demon can also expect to be stuck with the Inspired condition (or something similar, after all he DID do something incredible just then).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T12:44:17-08:00","id":55622,"title":"","content":"The primary problem with raising the dead over long periods isn't really the insane amount of successes needed, but whether or not the soul is even still available (unless you're putting in a new one).<br /> <br /> That being said, the extra necessary successes is at least in part related to body decomposition, because you get extra successes for embalmed bodies. If your players are going to the extreme of setting up someone with Swift Resolution so that they can use Raise Dead on someone who died a year ago, and they actually get the 370 or so successes -and- are willing to deal with the -15 to a Compromise roll that will probably spawn an Angel up their backside after they focus for two weeks? I don't see a reason to think too long over it. Raising the Dead isn't as consequential as people tend to think it is, in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}